237 0 obj
<<
/A 1955 0 R
/Alt (Six line graphs compare average temperature and hydrogen release for 316L stainless-steel, AlSi10Mg aluminium-alloy, and CuCr1Zr copper-alloy foams, each at varying porosities, with and without metal foam. Left panels \(a, c, e\) show increasing average temperature over time; right panels \(b, d, f\) display decreasing hydrogen concentration. A magenta curve labeled PG-SADE-GHF achieves fastest heat transfer and hydrogen release in all cases. Data sets are color-coded and identified in the legend. Each set of graphs shares similar trends, showing faster heating and hydrogen release at higher porosities and with the PG-SADE-GHF approach.)
/ID (ID.01106)
/K 1956 0 R
/P 16 0 R
/S /Figure
/Type /StructElem
>>
endobj
